<!--
  Kvertis colour tokens (ADR-017 in docs/03-architektur.md, table in docs/06-design.md).
  The hex values are taken 1:1 from the interface draft; mint is the only action colour, the kind colours
  (image, audio, video, document, model) carry meaning across all three steps.

  Structure per theme dictionary: first the Color values (Kv*Color), then the brushes (Kv*Brush), then the
  overrides for the WinUI accent resources so that standard controls (AccentButtonStyle, Slider, ToggleSwitch,
  CheckBox, RadioButton, ProgressBar, Hyperlink) wear mint without an extra style per control. The tokens and
  mixed brushes of the draft alignment (quiet, hover, frames, tints, panel/bg percentages, card gradient) and the
  colour overrides for the standard controls (secondary button, text fields, combo box, expander, focus ring) live
  here as well, because they are colours; the styles and templates that use them are in KvertisControls.xaml.

  High contrast: no own colour values at all. Every token is an alias of a system colour, and the accent
  overrides resolve to the same system colours WinUI itself uses there, so the result is identical to having
  no override. They are still listed, because a theme dictionary that omits a key can fall back to "Default".
-->
<ResourceDictionary
  xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
  xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <ResourceDictionary.ThemeDictionaries>

